            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A drug delivery ocular implant (53) comprising an outer shell (54) having a first end (52) and a second end (50), the outer shell (54) being shaped to define an interior lumen (58). The implant also comprises a cap (54a) comprising a central aperture defining a region of drug release (56), the cap (54a) fitted to the first end (52) of the outer shell (54), the region of drug release (56) configured to elute a drug. The implant also comprises a membrane (60) comprising elastic properties configured to retain the cap (54a) onto the outer shell (54).</p>
            </abstract>
